WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:02.540
This research program is about

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:05.200
building AIs,
and developing AIs

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.300
in places that big companies

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.520
aren't going to do it

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.580
and academic researchers
were focused on it, but there was a whole

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:19.720
missing middle of exciting opportunities and
applications that would help a lot of people

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:21.200
that weren't being developed.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:27.100
And so the impetus for this proposal was to
put that together.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:29.020
Basically in all of these big social

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:30.300
problems
whether it's education,

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:31.640
or health, or climate

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:33.180
where the problem is predicated

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:35.380
on uncertainty
and AIs that are

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:36.539
basically prediction tools

00:00:36.539 --> 00:00:38.280
can reduce the uncertainty

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:41.469
and benefit society
there's very few times in a person's lifetime

00:00:41.469 --> 00:00:44.969
where they have a chance to work on a problem
that can have such a big social impact.

00:00:44.969 --> 00:00:46.710
This is one of those times.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:52.140
CIFAR has a unique funding model through this
program that enables us to do 2 things, 1

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:58.210
is to work on a really hard problem over a
long period of time, so a lot of grant funding

00:00:58.210 --> 00:00:59.579
programs are much shorter.

00:00:59.579 --> 00:01:04.300
This one gives a very long runway, and it
enables multi-disciplinary.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:08.350
So the team we've put together where we have
domain expertise for example in public health

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:14.000
and medicine along with computer science expertise
particularly machine learning and AI, economics

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:23.700
expertise and psychology is a distinct group
that without CIFAR's patient model to deal

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:32.119
with complex research questions we will measure
whether this project is successful by the

00:01:32.119 --> 00:01:41.979
lives it impacts through helping control or
reduce the impact of climate change by - through

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:43.030
health and through education.

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:50.680
[Music]

